# @http against a local site (echo.py) that answers with the request it received.
# The reference is PennMUSH with pennmush/pennmush#1398 applied (tools/parity/patches/), which adds a
# headers argument and %q<http-overflow>; #1398 is not merged upstream.
# The imported world has http_qregisters on, so SharpMUSH reads and sets PennMUSH's q-registers here.
::case http.login
::login wiz Wiz wizpass
&HTTPCB me=think %q<status> %0 overflow=%q<http-overflow> HTTPDONE

::case http.get  a GET with no headers
::until HTTPDONE
@http me/HTTPCB={{echo}}/get

::case http.get-headers  a GET's headers follow the URL
::until HTTPDONE
@http me/HTTPCB={{echo}}/get,X-Parity:one

::case http.post-form  a body with no type goes out as a form
::until HTTPDONE
@http/post me/HTTPCB={{echo}}/post,a=1

::case http.post-headers  a Content-Type line sets the body's type; other lines are sent as written
::until HTTPDONE
@http/post me/HTTPCB={{echo}}/post,a=1,Content-Type:application/json

::case http.put-type-register  %q<content-type> sets the body's type when no headers are given
::until HTTPDONE
@http/put me/HTTPCB=[setq(content-type,text/csv)]{{echo}}/put,a=1

::case http.headers-over-register  given headers, %q<content-type> is not read
::until HTTPDONE
@http/post me/HTTPCB=[setq(content-type,text/csv)]{{echo}}/post,a=1,X-Parity:two

::case http.userpass  %q<userpass> logs in to a site that asks
::until HTTPDONE
@http me/HTTPCB=[setq(userpass,user:secret)]{{echo}}/auth

::case http.bad-header  a header line with no colon refuses the command
@http me/HTTPCB={{echo}}/get,nocolon
